| Course-level check 1, after unit 2 (week 12, course day 23; it stands for unit 2's end-of-unit assessment) | 2 | 1 | 1 | A 45-minute sitting with unseen items. Scores unit 2 in full: trace the values in a new algorithmic system's description and name one priority it trades away (HS-ALG-IM-11); evaluate the rationale, intended and unintended effects of a new law from a plain-language summary, naming its technical, legal or social approach (HS-SYS-IM-36); judge the efficacy of a new data policy from two short dated sources, with a social approach beside it (HS-DAT-IM-28), and name its effect on an under-represented group with the evidence and one fairer way to collect the data (S1-DSC-PP-13). Samples unit 1 with one new saved output to judge for accuracy and harm (HS-ALG-PS-05); unit 1's end-of-unit record for S1-AIN-HR-09 and HS-SOC-HU-44 is carried unscored. Written short answers and one paragraph. Course day 24, the respond day for unit 2 and the check, reteaches by error letter and repeats each missed item in a new form; its last ten minutes hold the readiness check for unit 3 (Course order) |
| Course-level check 2, year-end (week 28, course day 55; it stands for unit 4's end-of-unit assessment) | 4 | 1 | 1 | A 45-minute sitting with unseen items. Scores unit 4 in full: write the credits and permission notes for a new short program with a library, others' code, an image and a generated snippet, from license cards (HS-PRO-PD-14); from a new team's user-test notes and test results, choose the next change, say what it improves (function, use, access, accuracy or speed) and check it against the team's stated values (HS-PRO-TR-20); a heuristic review of a new printed screen for users of different abilities, languages and cultures, with two recommendations (S1-SWD-UX-05). Samples units 1 to 3 with three short new items: a saved output judged (HS-ALG-PS-05, unit 1), a policy's efficacy judged from one source (HS-DAT-IM-28, unit 2), a workflow fault found in a new design document and log (HS-PRO-PD-15, unit 3); unit 3's scored program and sitting are carried unscored. Course day 56, the respond day for unit 4 and the check, reteaches by error letter and records each student's gains. Unit 5 follows in weeks 29 to 32 and is checked by its own end-of-unit product |

