## Units

Unit order: the narrative first, while seniors write application essays; the year's hardest literary reading (Hamlet) early, while there is time for it, with its comic pair after; the 1920s once US History II has taught the decade; essays before speeches, speeches and a policy question before the law; the research project last, sharing its question with US History II's capstone. Day ranges follow the current scope and sequence.

