eminars led by students who set the goal, deadline and roles (SL.11-12.1a to d), with a partner talk one-on-one before each; the independent book chosen, Pride and Prejudice offered first; the unit word list and the student's own log. | Seniors write application essays in the fall: the course's first piece serves that use (a student may submit their own). Short texts let the year's routines start before Hamlet. Opens with an unmarked retrieval task on grade 11's two-viewpoint narrative and process routine (e11-narrative, e11-process). | Candidate: settled in the scope and sequence. Dropped: further reflective model and recent-memoir quotation, zero days; three anchors and original model suffice. | Students may write about hard experiences: they choose what to share, the teacher reads privately, and no student is asked to disclose; a disclosure goes to the school's support process. Keller and Hurston are grade 9's anchors and are not reread here. Sensitivity read, after the counselling and trauma guidance the brief names, for the writing task. |
